    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "eacabda8f08d2fa5174f977962936bde1cc7cbc26ab464726bb304100ffec37a",
      "text": "Breakfast. Group excursion with an English-speaking guide to the Perito Moreno Glacier, 80 km from El Calafate at the south-western end of Lago Argentino. Named after a great 19th-century Argentine explorer, it is one of the few glaciers in the world that is not retreating, and one of South America’s most spectacular natural shows: from time to time its 60-metre ice front releases walls of ice the size of buildings into Brazo Rico or the Canal de los Témpanos.\n\nPeriodically, the advancing glacier reaches the Magallanes Peninsula and divides the lake in two: Brazo Rico is dammed and its level rises considerably, until the water pierces the ice and the barrier collapses. A breathtaking show.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_aligned",
        "fileId": "1VVb19fhYM4uGHIUqj8Vb14ySVdLL-qs9",
        "documentSha256": "9fdbbd3080671e41cc722fff470a09cba94d9e99405241b2901cd1f0c38e2079",
